#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""A conversation's changes for the review view, and review feedback typed into its tmux pane.

Usage:
  ai-todo-review status <cwd> [--ref <branch>]
  ai-todo-review diff <cwd> [--scope uncommitted|branch|since] [--from <sha>] [--to <sha>]
                            [--unified N] [--max-bytes N] [--ref <branch>]
  ai-todo-review keep <cwd> <sha>
  ai-todo-review log <cwd> [--limit N] [--before <ISO time>] [--ref <branch>]
  ai-todo-review send [--base64] <tmux_name>   (the message on stdin)
  ai-todo-review run <cwd> --from <sha> --to <sha> --tool claude|codex --id <id> [--ref <branch>]
                         [--model M] [--context <path>]... [--brief-base64]   (the brief on stdin)
  ai-todo-review result <id>
  ai-todo-review cancel <id>
  ai-todo-review pr <cwd> [--ref <branch>] [--number N]
  ai-todo-review threads <cwd> [--ref <branch>] [--number N]
  ai-todo-review publish <cwd> --number N --head <sha>   (the review, base64 JSON, on stdin)
  ai-todo-review merge <cwd> --number N --head <sha> --method merge|squash|rebase [--delete-branch]

Every command but send prints JSON.

A revision is a commit sha. With nothing uncommitted it is HEAD. Otherwise it is a snapshot
commit on top of HEAD, made from a temporary index (`git add -A`), so untracked files are in
it and neither the real index, the working tree nor the stash stack is touched. The snapshot
has a fixed author, committer, date and message, so the same worktree gives the same sha.

status  root, branch, head, upstream with ahead/behind, the branch's base (merge-base with
        origin's default branch) and the current revision. worktree_base: when the repository
        is a worktree the runner or app made (runner-state/worktrees.json), the commit it was
        made from (its merge-base with HEAD, so a branch kept from an earlier worktree counts
        from where it began); else null.
--ref   reviews that branch of the repository instead of its working tree: HEAD is the
        branch's tip, the revision is that commit and nothing is uncommitted. For a
        conversation whose worktree is gone but whose branch is kept in the project folder.
diff    a unified diff of the repository (paths from its root) from --from to --to (default:
        the current revision). --scope picks --from: uncommitted = HEAD (default), branch = the
        base, since = --from as given. --unified 0 is for moving comments between revisions.
keep    refs/ai-review/<sha> -> sha, so a revision feedback was sent against survives gc.
log     HEAD's recent commits (first parent): sha, subject, committer date, and whether the
        upstream has it (null without an upstream). --before: also the last commit made before
        that time ("before"), the start of a conversation that began then; null when none was.
send    pastes stdin into the tmux session `<tmux_name>` as a bracketed paste, then Return.
        --base64: stdin is base64 (the app sends it so; decoding here needs no base64 flags).
        Paste end markers (ESC[201~) in the message are dropped, so it can't end the paste
        early. Refused (exit 75) while the program there hasn't turned bracketed paste on:
        line by line, every newline would submit.

run     starts a reviewer agent on the changes --from..--to, detached, and prints {"id", "state"}
        at once. claude runs as `claude -p` with only Read, Grep and Glob; codex as `codex exec`
        in its read-only sandbox. It reads the files as of --to, exported into the run's folder
        (the working tree may change while it reads). Context goes in
        as paths it may read: the brief (the todo's title and notes, base64 on stdin with
        --brief-base64), AGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md (the root's and those above changed files),
        docs/adr and spec folders, and every --context path. The run's files are in
        ~/.ai-remote/review-runs/<id> (AI_TODO_REVIEW_RUNS_DIR); runs older than 7 days go.
result  {"id", "state": running|done|failed|cancelled, "error", "result"}. A done run's result:
        tool, model, from, to, summary, usage (tokens and cost when the tool reports them, else
        null) and findings: path, side (new|old), line_start, line_end (null for the whole
        file), severity (high|medium|low), category, title, body, quote (the lines, from git,
        not the model) and fingerprint (path + title + nearby code, not line numbers, so the
        same finding on moved lines matches).
pr      the pull/merge request of the branch (GitHub with gh, GitLab with glab, by origin's URL or
        `git config ai-remote.forge`): {provider, access, error, viewer (who gh/glab act as),
        branch, pr}. pr: number, url, title, body, state (open|merged|closed), draft, author,
        review_decision, approvals, mergeable, checks {state passing|failing|pending|none, counts},
        head_sha, head_ref, base_ref; null when the branch has none. access false with error
        when the CLI is missing, logged out or failing: nothing else depends on it. Read-only.
threads its review threads on lines: {provider, access, error, pr, threads: [{id, path, side,
        line_start, line_end, commit, resolved, outdated, url, comments [{author, body,
        created_at}]}]}. GitHub: GraphQL reviewThreads; GitLab: the MR's discussions. The lines
        are in `commit`: the head (base for removed lines), or for an outdated GitHub thread
        the commit it was written on. --number with --url (GitHub) or --project (GitLab), as
        `pr` printed them, skips looking the PR up again.
publish posts a review on the PR/MR, as the computer's gh/glab account: {event COMMENT|APPROVE|
        REQUEST_CHANGES, body, comments [{path, side, line_start, line_end, body}]}, lines of
        --head. GitHub: one review against commit_id = --head, all or nothing. GitLab: one
        discussion per comment on the MR's diff refs (the user's own drafts stay drafts), the
        summary as a note, then approve with sha. Exit 67 when the head isn't --head any more.
merge   merges it through the API (nothing changes in the worktree) only while its head is
        --head, deleting the branch on the forge when asked. GitLab must answer merged: queued
        for a pipeline is a failure. Branch protection and checks are the forge's to enforce.
cancel  stops a running reviewer (its whole process group). Prints what `result` does: a run
        that finished first stays done, with its findings.

Exit codes: 64 bad arguments, 65 unknown revision or empty message (or nothing to publish),
67 the PR/MR moved on from --head, 77 gh/glab failed (their words on stderr), 78 some
GitLab comments were posted before a later step failed, 66 no such tmux
session, 69 not a git repository (or cwd missing), 70 git failed (its message on stderr),
75 the pane isn't ready for a paste, 90 git, tmux, claude or codex missing.
"""
import base64
import binascii
import hashlib
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import signal
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import time

SNAPSHOT_IDENT = {
    "GIT_AUTHOR_NAME": "ai-review", "GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL": "ai-review@localhost",
    "GIT_COMMITTER_NAME": "ai-review", "GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL": "ai-review@localhost",
    "GIT_AUTHOR_DATE": "@0 +0000", "GIT_COMMITTER_DATE": "@0 +0000",
}
SNAPSHOT_MESSAGE = "ai-review snapshot\n"
KEEP_PREFIX = "refs/ai-review/"
DEFAULT_MAX_BYTES = 4 * 1024 * 1024
# The user's git config must not change what is parsed: no colour, prefixes, external diffs.
DIFF_CONFIG = ["-c", "diff.noprefix=false", "-c", "diff.mnemonicPrefix=false",
               "-c", "diff.external=", "-c", "color.ui=never", "-c", "core.quotePath=false"]


def die(message, code):
    sys.stderr.write("ai-todo-review: %s\n" % message)
    sys.exit(code)


def die_missing(program):
    """Exit 90 with a bare `<program> not found`, the line the app reads the name from."""
    sys.stderr.write("%s not found\n" % program)
    sys.exit(90)


def git(cwd, *args, env=None, check=True, text=True):
    full_env = dict(os.environ)
    full_env.pop("GIT_DIR", None)
    full_env.pop("GIT_WORK_TREE", None)
    full_env.pop("GIT_INDEX_FILE", None)
    full_env["GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS"] = "0"
    if env:
        full_env.update(env)
    try:
        result = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", cwd] + list(args), stdout=subprocess.PIPE,
                                stderr=subprocess.PIPE, env=full_env)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        die_missing("git")
    if check and result.returncode != 0:
        raise GitError(result.stderr.decode("utf-8", "replace").strip())
    out = result.stdout
    return (out.decode("utf-8", "replace") if text else out), result.returncode


class GitError(Exception):
    pass


def line(cwd, *args):
    """First line of output, or None when the command fails."""
    try:
        out, _ = git(cwd, *args)
    except GitError:
        return None
    out = out.strip()
    return out.splitlines()[0] if out else None


def repo_root(cwd):
    path = os.path.expanduser(cwd)
    if not os.path.isdir(path):
        die("no folder %s" % cwd, 69)
    root = line(path, "rev-parse", "--show-toplevel")
    if not root:
        die("%s is not in a git repository" % cwd, 69)
    return root


def head_sha(root):
    return line(root, "rev-parse", "--verify", "-q", "HEAD^{commit}")


def snapshot(root):
    """(revision sha, clean). Built in a temporary index. The snapshot index of the last call
    (this worktree's `ai-review-index`, else the real index) seeds it, so files whose stat data
    didn't change, untracked ones included, aren't hashed again. Calls at the same time each
    work on their own copy; the last one to finish leaves its index for the next."""
    head = head_sha(root)
    index = line(root, "rev-parse", "--path-format=absolute", "--git-path", "index")
    kept = line(root, "rev-parse", "--path-format=absolute", "--git-path", "ai-review-index")
    tmpdir = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="ai-review-", dir=os.path.dirname(kept) if kept else None)
    try:
        tmp_index = os.path.join(tmpdir, "index")
        seed = kept if kept and os.path.exists(kept) else index
        if seed and os.path.exists(seed):
            # copy2 keeps the mtime: git re-checks entries as new as the index (racy-git)
            shutil.copy2(seed, tmp_index)
        env = {"GIT_INDEX_FILE": tmp_index}
        git(root, "add", "-A", "--", ".", env=env)
        tree, _ = git(root, "write-tree", env=env)
        tree = tree.strip()
        if kept:
            try:
                os.replace(tmp_index, kept)
            except OSError:
                pass
    finally:
        shutil.rmtree(tmpdir, ignore_errors=True)
    if head and line(root, "rev-parse", head + "^{tree}") == tree:
        return head, True
    args = ["commit-tree", tree, "-m", SNAPSHOT_MESSAGE.strip()]
    if head:
        args[2:2] = ["-p", head]
    env = dict(SNAPSHOT_IDENT)
    sha, _ = git(root, *args, env=env)
    return sha.strip(), False


def default_branch_ref(root):
    ref = line(root, "symbolic-ref", "-q", "refs/remotes/origin/HEAD")
    candidates = ([ref] if ref else []) + ["refs/remotes/origin/main", "refs/remotes/origin/master",
                                           "refs/heads/main", "refs/heads/master"]
    for candidate in candidates:
        if line(root, "rev-parse", "--verify", "-q", candidate):
            return candidate
    return None


def short_ref(ref):
    for prefix in ("refs/remotes/", "refs/heads/"):
        if ref.startswith(prefix):
            return ref[len(prefix):]
    return ref


def base_of(root, head):
    ref = default_branch_ref(root)
    if not ref or not head:
        return None
    sha = line(root, "merge-base", head, ref)
    return {"ref": short_ref(ref), "sha": sha} if sha else None


def registry_file():
    state = os.environ.get("AI_TODO_RUNNER_STATE_DIR") or os.path.join(os.path.expanduser("~"), ".ai-remote", "runner-state")
    return os.path.join(state, "worktrees.json")


def worktree_base(root, head):
    """The commit this worktree was made from, when the runner or app made it; else None."""
    try:
        with open(registry_file()) as handle:
            registry = json.load(handle)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None
    entries = registry.values() if isinstance(registry, dict) else registry if isinstance(registry, list) else []
    real = os.path.realpath(root)
    for entry in entries:
        if not isinstance(entry, dict) or not entry.get("base") or not entry.get("path"):
            continue
        if os.path.realpath(entry["path"]) != real:
            continue
        base = line(root, "rev-parse", "--verify", "-q", entry["base"] + "^{commit}")
        if not base:
            return None
        return (line(root, "merge-base", base, head) if head else None) or base
    return None


def ref_sha(root, ref):
    """The tip of branch `ref`, or exit 65 when the repository has no such branch."""
    sha = line(root, "rev-parse", "--verify", "-q", "refs/heads/%s^{commit}" % ref)
    if not sha:
        die("no branch %s" % ref, 65)
    return sha


def take_ref(args):
    """(args without `--ref X`, X or None)."""
    rest = list(args)
    if "--ref" not in rest:
        return rest, None
    at = rest.index("--ref")
    if at + 1 >= len(rest) or not rest[at + 1] or rest[at + 1].startswith("-"):
        die("--ref needs a branch", 64)
    ref = rest[at + 1]
    del rest[at:at + 2]
    return rest, ref


def cmd_status(args):
    args, ref = take_ref(args)
    if len(args) != 1:
        die("usage: ai-todo-review status <cwd> [--ref <branch>]", 64)
    root = repo_root(args[0])
    if ref:
        head = ref_sha(root, ref)
        branch = ref
        upstream = line(root, "rev-parse", "--abbrev-ref", "--symbolic-full-name", "refs/heads/%s@{upstream}" % ref)
    else:
        head = head_sha(root)
        branch = line(root, "symbolic-ref", "-q", "--short", "HEAD")
        upstream = line(root, "rev-parse", "--abbrev-ref", "--symbolic-full-name", "@{upstream}")
    ahead = behind = None
    if upstream and head:
        counts = line(root, "rev-list", "--left-right", "--count", "%s...%s" % (head, upstream))
        if counts and len(counts.split()) == 2:
            ahead, behind = (int(n) for n in counts.split())
    revision, clean = (head, True) if ref else snapshot(root)
    print(json.dumps({
        "root": root,
        "branch": branch,
        "head": head,
        "upstream": upstream,
        "ahead": ahead,
        "behind": behind,
        "base": base_of(root, head),
        "revision": revision,
        "clean": clean,
        "worktree_base": None if ref else worktree_base(root, head),
        "ref": ref,
    }))


def cmd_diff(args):
    args, ref = take_ref(args)
    cwd = None
    scope = "uncommitted"
    from_sha = to_sha = None
    unified = 3
    max_bytes = DEFAULT_MAX_BYTES
    rest = list(args)
    try:
        while rest:
            arg = rest.pop(0)
            if arg == "--scope":
                scope = rest.pop(0)
            elif arg == "--from":
                from_sha = rest.pop(0)
            elif arg == "--to":
                to_sha = rest.pop(0)
            elif arg == "--unified":
                unified = int(rest.pop(0))
            elif arg == "--max-bytes":
                max_bytes = int(rest.pop(0))
            elif arg.startswith("-") or cwd is not None:
                raise ValueError(arg)
            else:
                cwd = arg
    except (IndexError, ValueError):
        die("usage: ai-todo-review diff <cwd> [--scope uncommitted|branch|since] [--from <sha>] "
            "[--to <sha>] [--unified N] [--max-bytes N]", 64)
    if cwd is None or scope not in ("uncommitted", "branch", "since") or unified < 0 or max_bytes < 1:
        die("usage: ai-todo-review diff <cwd> [--scope uncommitted|branch|since] ...", 64)
    root = repo_root(cwd)
    head = ref_sha(root, ref) if ref else head_sha(root)
    if to_sha is None:
        to_sha = head if ref else snapshot(root)[0]
    if scope == "since":
        if not from_sha:
            die("--scope since needs --from <sha>", 64)
    elif scope == "branch":
        base = base_of(root, head)
        from_sha = base["sha"] if base else head
    elif from_sha is None:
        from_sha = head
    for sha in (from_sha, to_sha):
        if sha and not line(root, "rev-parse", "--verify", "-q", sha + "^{commit}"):
            die("unknown revision %s" % sha, 65)
    if from_sha is None:
        # No commits yet: everything is new.
        from_sha = line(root, "hash-object", "-t", "tree", "/dev/null")
    # Explicit prefixes: diff.srcPrefix / diff.dstPrefix (git 2.45+) would change them.
    patch, _ = git(root, *DIFF_CONFIG, "diff", "--no-color", "--no-ext-diff", "--no-textconv",
                   "--src-prefix=a/", "--dst-prefix=b/", "-M", "--unified=%d" % unified, from_sha, to_sha, "--", text=False)
    truncated = len(patch) > max_bytes
    if truncated:
        cut = patch.rfind(b"\ndiff --git ", 0, max_bytes)
        # Whole files only: a file cut mid-hunk would move comments as if its tail were unchanged.
        patch = patch[:cut + 1] if cut > 0 else b""
    print(json.dumps({
        "from": from_sha,
        "to": to_sha,
        "scope": scope,
        "patch": patch.decode("utf-8", "replace"),
        "truncated": truncated,
    }))


def cmd_log(args):
    args, ref = take_ref(args)
    limit = 30
    before = None
    rest = list(args)
    cwd = None
    try:
        while rest:
            arg = rest.pop(0)
            if arg == "--limit":
                limit = int(rest.pop(0))
            elif arg == "--before":
                before = rest.pop(0)
            elif arg.startswith("-") or cwd is not None:
                raise ValueError(arg)
            else:
                cwd = arg
    except (IndexError, ValueError):
        cwd = None
    if cwd is None or not 1 <= limit <= 500 or (before is not None and not before.strip()):
        die("usage: ai-todo-review log <cwd> [--limit N] [--before <ISO time>]", 64)
    root = repo_root(cwd)
    head = ref_sha(root, ref) if ref else head_sha(root)
    commits = []
    found_before = None
    if head:
        out, _ = git(root, "log", "--first-parent", "-n", str(limit), "--format=%H%x1f%s%x1f%cI", head)
        unpushed = None
        upstream = line(root, "rev-parse", "--abbrev-ref", "--symbolic-full-name",
                        ("refs/heads/%s@{upstream}" % ref) if ref else "@{upstream}")
        if upstream:
            listed, _ = git(root, "rev-list", "%s..%s" % (upstream, head))
            unpushed = set(listed.split())
        for row in out.splitlines():
            parts = row.split("\x1f")
            if len(parts) != 3:
                continue
            sha, subject, date = parts
            commits.append({"sha": sha, "subject": subject, "date": date,
                            "pushed": None if unpushed is None else sha not in unpushed})
        if before is not None:
            found_before = line(root, "rev-list", "--first-parent", "-n", "1", "--before=" + before, head)
    print(json.dumps({"commits": commits, "before": found_before}))


def cmd_keep(args):
    if len(args) != 2:
        die("usage: ai-todo-review keep <cwd> <sha>", 64)
    root = repo_root(args[0])
    sha = line(root, "rev-parse", "--verify", "-q", args[1] + "^{commit}")
    if not sha:
        die("unknown revision %s" % args[1], 65)
    git(root, "update-ref", KEEP_PREFIX + sha, sha)
    print(json.dumps({"kept": sha}))


def tmux(*args, stdin=None):
    socket = os.environ.get("AI_TODO_TMUX_SOCKET")
    command = ["tmux"] + (["-L", socket] if socket else []) + list(args)
    try:
        return subprocess.run(command, input=stdin, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        die_missing("tmux")


PASTE_END = b"\x1b[201~"
PASTE_SETTLE_SECONDS = float(os.environ.get("AI_TODO_REVIEW_PASTE_SETTLE", "0.3"))


def cmd_send(args):
    encoded = bool(args) and args[0] == "--base64"
    if encoded:
        args = args[1:]
    if len(args) != 1 or not args[0]:
        die("usage: ai-todo-review send [--base64] <tmux_name> < message", 64)
    name = args[0]
    message = sys.stdin.buffer.read()
    if encoded:
        try:
            message = base64.b64decode(message.strip(), validate=True)
        except (binascii.Error, ValueError):
            die("the message isn't base64", 64)
    # Removing one marker can join the pieces around it into another.
    while PASTE_END in message:
        message = message.replace(PASTE_END, b"")
    if not message.strip():
        die("empty message", 65)
    if tmux("has-session", "-t", "=" + name).returncode != 0:
        die("no tmux session %s" % name, 66)
    # The tool runs in the session's first pane (ai-todo-open starts it there). Not the active
    # one: a shell opened beside it would run the feedback as commands.
    panes = tmux("list-panes", "-s", "-t", "=" + name, "-F", "#{window_index} #{pane_index} #{pane_id}")
    rows = []
    for row in panes.stdout.decode().splitlines():
        parts = row.split()
        if len(parts) == 3 and parts[0].isdigit() and parts[1].isdigit():
            rows.append((int(parts[0]), int(parts[1]), parts[2]))
    if panes.returncode != 0 or not rows:
        die("no pane in %s" % name, 66)
    target = min(rows)[2]
    # "1": the program turned bracketed paste on. Empty: a tmux without this format (unknown),
    # where the agent, once running, has it on.
    flag = tmux("display-message", "-p", "-t", target, "#{bracket_paste_flag}")
    if flag.returncode != 0 or flag.stdout.decode().strip() not in ("1", ""):
        die("%s isn't ready for a paste" % name, 75)
    buffer = "ai-review-%d" % os.getpid()
    if tmux("load-buffer", "-b", buffer, "-", stdin=message.rstrip(b"\n")).returncode != 0:
        die("couldn't load the message into tmux", 75)
    pasted = tmux("paste-buffer", "-p", "-d", "-b", buffer, "-t", target)
    if pasted.returncode != 0:
        tmux("delete-buffer", "-b", buffer)
        die("couldn't paste into %s" % name, 75)
    # A TUI may still be taking in a long paste; Return inside that would only add a line.
    time.sleep(PASTE_SETTLE_SECONDS)
    tmux("send-keys", "-t", target, "Enter")
    print(json.dumps({"sent": len(message)}))


# --- pull / merge requests (read-only) -------------------------------------------------

FORGE_TIMEOUT = float(os.environ.get("AI_TODO_REVIEW_FORGE_TIMEOUT", "30"))
CHECK_FAILED = {"FAILURE", "TIMED_OUT", "CANCELLED", "ACTION_REQUIRED", "STARTUP_FAILURE", "ERROR", "STALE"}

GITHUB_THREADS = """
query($owner: String!, $name: String!, $number: Int!) {
  repository(owner: $owner, name: $name) {
    pullRequest(number: $number) {
      baseRefOid headRefOid
      reviewThreads(first: 100) {
        nodes {
          id isResolved isOutdated path line startLine originalLine originalStartLine diffSide
          comments(first: 50) {
            nodes { author { login } body createdAt url commit { oid } originalCommit { oid } }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}"""


class NoAccess(Exception):
    """The forge's CLI is missing, logged out, or can't reach it."""


def workspace_module():
    """ai_todo_workspace, installed next to this script: the runner's forge and PR lookup."""
    sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)))
    import ai_todo_workspace
    return ai_todo_workspace


def forge_kind(root):
    """github | gitlab | None, as the runner decides it."""
    return workspace_module().forge(root)


def find_number(kind, root, branch):
    """The number of the branch's PR/MR the runner would pick (an open one, else the latest),
    or None. NoAccess, with why, when the CLI can't be asked."""
    workspace = workspace_module()
    try:
        found = workspace.find_pr(root, branch)
    except workspace.PRUnknown:
        # find_pr says only that it failed: ask once more to say why (missing, logged out).
        forge_json(kind, root, "api", "user")
        raise NoAccess("%s couldn't list the pull requests" % os.path.basename(forge_cli(kind)))
    return found.get("number") if found else None


def forge_cli(kind):
    name = "gh" if kind == "github" else "glab"
    return os.environ.get("AI_TODO_GH_BIN" if kind == "github" else "AI_TODO_GLAB_BIN") or shutil.which(name) or name


def forge_json(kind, root, *args):
    """The CLI's JSON answer, or NoAccess with why."""
    binary = forge_cli(kind)
    try:
        p = subprocess.run([binary] + list(args), cwd=root, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE,
                           stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, timeout=FORGE_TIMEOUT)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        raise NoAccess("%s isn't installed" % os.path.basename(binary))
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        raise NoAccess("%s didn't answer in %d s" % (os.path.basename(binary), FORGE_TIMEOUT))
    err = p.stderr.decode("utf-8", "replace").strip()
    if p.returncode != 0:
        lowered = err.lower()
        if "auth" in lowered or "login" in lowered or "401" in lowered or "token" in lowered:
            raise NoAccess("%s isn't logged in" % os.path.basename(binary))
        raise NoAccess("%s failed: %s" % (os.path.basename(binary), (err.splitlines() or [""])[-1][:200]))
    try:
        return json.loads(p.stdout.decode("utf-8", "replace") or "null")
    except ValueError:
        raise NoAccess("%s's answer wasn't JSON" % os.path.basename(binary))


def checks_summary(rollup):
    """{state: passing|failing|pending|none, passed, failed, pending, total} of GitHub's rollup."""
    passed = failed = pending = 0
    for check in rollup or []:
        if not isinstance(check, dict):
            continue
        if check.get("__typename") == "StatusContext" or "state" in check and "status" not in check:
            state = str(check.get("state") or "").upper()
            if state == "SUCCESS":
                passed += 1
            elif state in ("PENDING", "EXPECTED"):
                pending += 1
            else:
                failed += 1
            continue
        if str(check.get("status") or "").upper() != "COMPLETED":
            pending += 1
        elif str(check.get("conclusion") or "").upper() in CHECK_FAILED:
            failed += 1
        else:
            passed += 1
    total = passed + failed + pending
    state = "none" if total == 0 else "failing" if failed else "pending" if pending else "passing"
    return {"state": state, "passed": passed, "failed": failed, "pending": pending, "total": total}


def pipeline_summary(status):
    """GitLab's head pipeline status as the same summary."""
    status = str(status or "").lower()
    if not status:
        return {"state": "none", "passed": 0, "failed": 0, "pending": 0, "total": 0}
    state = {"success": "passing", "failed": "failing", "canceled": "failing"}.get(status, "pending")
    return {"state": state, "passed": int(state == "passing"), "failed": int(state == "failing"),
            "pending": int(state == "pending"), "total": 1}


def branch_for(root, ref):
    return ref or line(root, "symbolic-ref", "-q", "--short", "HEAD")


def github_pr(root, branch, number):
    if number is None:
        number = find_number("github", root, branch)
        if number is None:
            return None
    view = forge_json("github", root, "pr", "view", str(number), "--json",
                      "number,url,title,body,state,isDraft,author,reviewDecision,mergeStateStatus,mergeable,"
                      "statusCheckRollup,headRefOid,headRefName,baseRefName,latestReviews")
    if not isinstance(view, dict):
        return None
    approvals = sorted({(r.get("author") or {}).get("login") for r in view.get("latestReviews") or []
                        if isinstance(r, dict) and r.get("state") == "APPROVED"} - {None})
    return {
        "number": view.get("number"), "url": view.get("url"), "title": view.get("title") or "",
        "body": view.get("body") or "", "state": str(view.get("state") or "").lower(),
        "draft": bool(view.get("isDraft")), "author": (view.get("author") or {}).get("login"),
        "review_decision": (view.get("reviewDecision") or "").lower() or None, "approvals": approvals,
        "mergeable": (view.get("mergeStateStatus") or view.get("mergeable") or "").lower() or None,
        "checks": checks_summary(view.get("statusCheckRollup")), "head_sha": view.get("headRefOid"),
        "head_ref": view.get("headRefName"), "base_ref": view.get("baseRefName"),
    }


def gitlab_pr(root, branch, number):
    if number is None:
        number = find_number("gitlab", root, branch)
        if number is None:
            return None
    view = forge_json("gitlab", root, "mr", "view", str(number), "-F", "json")
    if not isinstance(view, dict):
        return None
    approvals = []
    decision = None
    project = view.get("project_id")
    if project:
        try:
            data = forge_json("gitlab", root, "api", "projects/%s/merge_requests/%s/approvals" % (project, number)) or {}
            approvals = sorted({((a or {}).get("user") or {}).get("username") for a in data.get("approved_by") or []} - {None})
            # Approved only when the MR's approval rules are met, not at the first approval.
            if data.get("approved") is True or (data.get("approvals_left") == 0 and approvals):
                decision = "approved"
            elif (data.get("approvals_left") or 0) > 0:
                decision = "review_required"
        except NoAccess:
            pass
    state = {"opened": "open", "locked": "open"}.get(view.get("state"), view.get("state") or "")
    return {
        "number": view.get("iid"), "url": view.get("web_url"), "title": view.get("title") or "",
        "body": view.get("description") or "", "state": state,
        "draft": bool(view.get("draft") or view.get("work_in_progress")),
        "author": (view.get("author") or {}).get("username"),
        "review_decision": decision, "approvals": approvals,
        "mergeable": (view.get("detailed_merge_status") or view.get("merge_status") or "").lower() or None,
        "checks": pipeline_summary((view.get("head_pipeline") or view.get("pipeline") or {}).get("status")),
        "head_sha": view.get("sha"), "head_ref": view.get("source_branch"), "base_ref": view.get("target_branch"),
        "project_id": project,
    }


def viewer(kind, root):
    try:
        user = forge_json(kind, root, "api", "user")
    except NoAccess:
        return None
    if not isinstance(user, dict):
        return None
    return user.get("login") if kind == "github" else user.get("username")


def take_number(args):
    rest = list(args)
    if "--number" not in rest:
        return rest, None
    at = rest.index("--number")
    try:
        number = int(rest[at + 1])
    except (IndexError, ValueError):
        die("--number needs a number", 64)
    del rest[at:at + 2]
    return rest, number


def take_option(args, name):
    rest = list(args)
    if name not in rest:
        return rest, None
    at = rest.index(name)
    if at + 1 >= len(rest) or not rest[at + 1]:
        die("%s needs a value" % name, 64)
    value = rest[at + 1]
    del rest[at:at + 2]
    return rest, value


def forge_context(args, usage):
    args, ref = take_ref(args)
    args, number = take_number(args)
    args, url = take_option(args, "--url")
    args, project = take_option(args, "--project")
    if len(args) != 1:
        die(usage, 64)
    root = repo_root(args[0])
    branch = branch_for(root, ref)
    return root, branch, number, forge_kind(root), url, project


def cmd_pr(args):
    root, branch, number, kind, _, _ = forge_context(args, "usage: ai-todo-review pr <cwd> [--ref <branch>] [--number N]")
    out = {"provider": kind, "access": False, "error": None, "viewer": None, "branch": branch, "pr": None}
    if kind is None:
        out["error"] = "origin is neither GitHub nor GitLab"
    elif not branch and number is None:
        # A detached HEAD has no PR of its own; that's not an access problem.
        out["access"] = True
    else:
        try:
            out["pr"] = (github_pr if kind == "github" else gitlab_pr)(root, branch, number)
            out["access"] = True
            out["viewer"] = viewer(kind, root)
        except NoAccess as error:
            out["error"] = str(error)
    print(json.dumps(out))


def github_threads(root, pr):
    m = re.match(r"https://[^/]+/([^/]+)/([^/]+)/pull/(\d+)", pr.get("url") or "")
    if not m:
        return []
    data = forge_json("github", root, "api", "graphql", "-f", "query=" + GITHUB_THREADS,
                      "-F", "owner=" + m.group(1), "-F", "name=" + m.group(2), "-F", "number=" + m.group(3))
    request = (((data or {}).get("data") or {}).get("repository") or {}).get("pullRequest") or {}
    nodes = request.get("reviewThreads") or {}
    threads = []
    for node in nodes.get("nodes") or []:
        comments = ((node or {}).get("comments") or {}).get("nodes") or []
        if not comments or not node.get("path"):
            continue
        first = comments[0]
        old_side = node.get("diffSide") == "LEFT"
        if node.get("line"):
            # Current: lines of the PR's head (or its base, for removed lines).
            line_no, start = node["line"], node.get("startLine") or node["line"]
            commit = request.get("baseRefOid") if old_side else request.get("headRefOid")
        else:
            # Outdated: where it was written, on the commit it was written on.
            line_no = node.get("originalLine")
            start = node.get("originalStartLine") or line_no
            commit = request.get("baseRefOid") if old_side else (first.get("originalCommit") or {}).get("oid")
        threads.append({
            "id": node.get("id"), "path": node["path"],
            "side": "old" if old_side else "new",
            "line_start": start, "line_end": line_no,
            "commit": commit,
            "resolved": bool(node.get("isResolved")), "outdated": bool(node.get("isOutdated")),
            "url": first.get("url"),
            "comments": [{"author": (c.get("author") or {}).get("login") or "ghost", "body": c.get("body") or "",
                          "created_at": c.get("createdAt")} for c in comments],
        })
    return threads


def gitlab_threads(root, pr):
    project = pr.get("project_id")
    if not project:
        return []
    data = forge_json("gitlab", root, "api", "projects/%s/merge_requests/%s/discussions?per_page=100" % (project, pr["number"]))
    threads = []
    for discussion in data or []:
        notes = [n for n in (discussion or {}).get("notes") or [] if isinstance(n, dict) and not n.get("system")]
        positioned = [n for n in notes if isinstance(n.get("position"), dict)]
        if not positioned:
            continue
        position = positioned[0]["position"]
        new_line, old_line = position.get("new_line"), position.get("old_line")
        side = "new" if new_line else "old"
        line_no = new_line or old_line
        start = line_no
        range_start = ((position.get("line_range") or {}).get("start") or {})
        if range_start.get("new_line" if side == "new" else "old_line"):
            start = range_start.get("new_line" if side == "new" else "old_line")
        threads.append({
            "id": discussion.get("id"),
            "path": position.get("new_path") if side == "new" else position.get("old_path") or position.get("new_path"),
            "side": side, "line_start": start, "line_end": line_no,
            "commit": position.get("head_sha") if side == "new" else position.get("base_sha"),
            "resolved": all(n.get("resolved") for n in notes if n.get("resolvable")) and any(n.get("resolvable") for n in notes),
            "outdated": False, "url": (pr.get("url") or "") + "#note_%s" % notes[0].get("id"),
            "comments": [{"author": (n.get("author") or {}).get("username") or "ghost", "body": n.get("body") or "",
                          "created_at": n.get("created_at")} for n in notes],
        })
    return threads


def cmd_threads(args):
    root, branch, number, kind, url, project = forge_context(
        args, "usage: ai-todo-review threads <cwd> [--ref <branch>] [--number N [--url U | --project P]]")
    out = {"provider": kind, "access": False, "error": None, "pr": None, "threads": []}
    if kind is None:
        out["error"] = "origin is neither GitHub nor GitLab"
    else:
        try:
            if number is not None and (url if kind == "github" else project):
                # What `pr` already said: one call for the threads, no second look at the PR.
                pr = {"number": number, "url": url, "project_id": project}
            else:
                pr = (github_pr if kind == "github" else gitlab_pr)(root, branch, number) if (branch or number) else None
            out["access"] = True
            if pr:
                out["pr"] = pr["number"]
                out["threads"] = (github_threads if kind == "github" else gitlab_threads)(root, pr)
        except NoAccess as error:
            out["access"] = False
            out["error"] = str(error)
    print(json.dumps(out))


# --- pull / merge requests: writes (each one confirmed in the app) --------------------

class HeadMoved(Exception):
    pass


def forge_call(kind, root, *args, stdin=None):
    """Runs a write; its JSON answer (or None). Exit 77 with the CLI's words when it fails."""
    binary = forge_cli(kind)
    try:
        p = subprocess.run([binary] + list(args), cwd=root, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE,
                           input=stdin, timeout=FORGE_TIMEOUT * 2)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        die("%s isn't installed" % os.path.basename(binary), 77)
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        die("%s didn't answer" % os.path.basename(binary), 77)
    if p.returncode != 0:
        err = p.stderr.decode("utf-8", "replace").strip() or p.stdout.decode("utf-8", "replace").strip()
        die("%s failed: %s" % (os.path.basename(binary), " ".join(err.split())[:300]), 77)
    try:
        return json.loads(p.stdout.decode("utf-8", "replace") or "null")
    except ValueError:
        return None


def write_context(args, usage):
    """(root, kind, number, head) for a write: --number and --head are required."""
    args, number = take_number(args)
    args, head = take_option(args, "--head")
    if number is None or not head or len(args) != 1 or args[0].startswith("-"):
        die(usage, 64)
    root = repo_root(args[0])
    kind = forge_kind(root)
    if kind is None:
        die("origin is neither GitHub nor GitLab", 64)
    return root, kind, number, head


def github_repo(kind, root, number):
    view = forge_call(kind, root, "pr", "view", str(number), "--json", "url,headRefOid,state")
    m = re.match(r"https://[^/]+/([^/]+)/([^/]+)/pull/\d+", (view or {}).get("url") or "")
    if not m:
        die("couldn't tell the repository of PR %s" % number, 77)
    return m.group(1), m.group(2), view


def gitlab_mr(root, number):
    view = forge_call("gitlab", root, "mr", "view", str(number), "-F", "json") or {}
    if not view.get("project_id"):
        die("couldn't tell the project of MR %s" % number, 77)
    detail = forge_call("gitlab", root, "api", "projects/%s/merge_requests/%s" % (view["project_id"], number)) or {}
    view["diff_refs"] = detail.get("diff_refs") or {}
    return view


def cmd_publish(args):
    """publish <cwd> --number N --head SHA: the review JSON, base64, on stdin:
    {event: COMMENT|APPROVE|REQUEST_CHANGES, body, comments: [{path, old_path, side, line_start,
    line_end, old_line, body}]}. Refused (67) when the PR's head isn't SHA any more: the
    comments' lines are lines of SHA."""
    root, kind, number, head = write_context(args, "usage: ai-todo-review publish <cwd> --number N --head <sha> < review")
    try:
        review = json.loads(base64.b64decode(sys.stdin.buffer.read().strip(), validate=True))
    except (binascii.Error, ValueError):
        die("the review isn't base64 JSON", 64)
    event = review.get("event") or "COMMENT"
    if event not in ("COMMENT", "APPROVE", "REQUEST_CHANGES"):
        die("bad event %s" % event, 64)
    comments = [c for c in review.get("comments") or [] if isinstance(c, dict) and c.get("path") and c.get("body")]
    body = (review.get("body") or "").strip()
    if event == "REQUEST_CHANGES" and not body:
        die("Request Changes needs a summary", 64)
    if event == "COMMENT" and not body and not comments:
        die("nothing to publish", 65)
    if kind == "github":
        owner, name, view = github_repo(kind, root, number)
        if view.get("headRefOid") != head:
            die("PR %s moved on to %s" % (number, (view.get("headRefOid") or "")[:8]), 67)
        # One review, posted at once: all of it or none of it.
        payload = {"commit_id": head, "event": event, "body": body, "comments": []}
        for c in comments:
            item = {"path": c["path"], "body": c["body"], "line": c.get("line_end") or c.get("line_start"),
                    "side": "LEFT" if c.get("side") == "old" else "RIGHT"}
            if c.get("line_start") and c.get("line_end") and c["line_end"] != c["line_start"]:
                item["start_line"] = c["line_start"]
                item["start_side"] = item["side"]
            payload["comments"].append(item)
        answer = forge_call(kind, root, "api", "-X", "POST", "repos/%s/%s/pulls/%s/reviews" % (owner, name, number),
                            "--input", "-", stdin=json.dumps(payload).encode("utf-8"))
        print(json.dumps({"published": len(payload["comments"]), "event": event, "url": (answer or {}).get("html_url")}))
        return
    view = gitlab_mr(root, number)
    refs = view["diff_refs"]
    if view.get("sha") != head or refs.get("head_sha") not in (None, head):
        die("MR %s moved on to %s" % (number, (view.get("sha") or "")[:8]), 67)
    if event == "REQUEST_CHANGES":
        die("GitLab has no request-changes review; publish comments instead", 64)
    base = "projects/%s/merge_requests/%s" % (view["project_id"], number)
    # Each comment is its own discussion, posted at once: the user's own pending drafts on
    # GitLab stay drafts. A failure part way says how many went.
    posted = 0
    for c in comments:
        text = c["body"]
        if c.get("line_start") and c.get("line_end") and c["line_end"] != c["line_start"]:
            text = "(lines %d-%d) %s" % (c["line_start"], c["line_end"], text)
        line_no = c.get("line_end") or c.get("line_start")
        fields = ["-f", "body=" + text, "-f", "position[position_type]=text",
                  "-f", "position[base_sha]=" + (refs.get("base_sha") or ""),
                  "-f", "position[start_sha]=" + (refs.get("start_sha") or ""),
                  "-f", "position[head_sha]=" + head,
                  "-f", "position[new_path]=" + c["path"], "-f", "position[old_path]=" + (c.get("old_path") or c["path"])]
        if c.get("side") == "old":
            fields += ["-F", "position[old_line]=%d" % line_no]
        else:
            fields += ["-F", "position[new_line]=%d" % line_no]
            # An unchanged line is on both sides: GitLab wants both numbers.
            if c.get("old_line"):
                fields += ["-F", "position[old_line]=%d" % c["old_line"]]
        partial_call(root, posted, len(comments), "api", "-X", "POST", base + "/discussions", *fields)
        posted += 1
    if body:
        partial_call(root, posted, len(comments), "api", "-X", "POST", base + "/notes", "-f", "body=" + body)
    if event == "APPROVE":
        partial_call(root, posted, len(comments), "api", "-X", "POST", base + "/approve", "-f", "sha=" + head,
                     what="the approval")
    print(json.dumps({"published": posted, "event": event, "url": view.get("web_url")}))


def partial_call(root, posted, total, *args, what="it"):
    """A GitLab write after `posted` of `total` comments went: a failure says so (exit 78)."""
    binary = forge_cli("gitlab")
    try:
        p = subprocess.run([binary] + list(args), cwd=root, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE,
                           stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, timeout=FORGE_TIMEOUT * 2)
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as error:
        p, err = None, type(error).__name__
    else:
        err = " ".join((p.stderr.decode("utf-8", "replace") or p.stdout.decode("utf-8", "replace")).split())[:300]
    if p is not None and p.returncode == 0:
        return
    if posted == 0:
        die("glab failed: %s" % err, 77)
    die("%d of %d comments are posted on GitLab; %s failed: %s" % (posted, total, what, err), 78)


def cmd_merge(args):
    """merge <cwd> --number N --head SHA --method merge|squash|rebase [--delete-branch]: through
    the forge's API, only while the PR's head is SHA; nothing changes in the worktree."""
    args, method = take_option(args, "--method")
    delete_branch = "--delete-branch" in args
    args = [a for a in args if a != "--delete-branch"]
    root, kind, number, head = write_context(
        args, "usage: ai-todo-review merge <cwd> --number N --head <sha> --method merge|squash|rebase [--delete-branch]")
    if method not in ("merge", "squash", "rebase"):
        die("--method must be merge, squash or rebase", 64)
    if kind == "github":
        owner, name, view = github_repo(kind, root, number)
        answer = forge_call(kind, root, "api", "-X", "PUT", "repos/%s/%s/pulls/%s/merge" % (owner, name, number),
                            "-f", "sha=" + head, "-f", "merge_method=" + method) or {}
        if answer.get("merged") is not True:
            die("GitHub didn't merge it (%s)" % (answer.get("message") or "no answer"), 77)
        deleted = False
        if delete_branch:
            branch = forge_call(kind, root, "pr", "view", str(number), "--json", "headRefName") or {}
            if branch.get("headRefName"):
                forge_call(kind, root, "api", "-X", "DELETE",
                           "repos/%s/%s/git/refs/heads/%s" % (owner, name, branch["headRefName"]))
                deleted = True
        print(json.dumps({"merged": number, "method": method, "deleted_branch": deleted}))
        return
    if method == "rebase":
        die("GitLab merges with a merge commit or a squash here", 64)
    view = gitlab_mr(root, number)
    answer = forge_call("gitlab", root, "api", "-X", "PUT",
                        "projects/%s/merge_requests/%s/merge" % (view["project_id"], number),
                        "-f", "sha=" + head, "-F", "squash=%s" % ("true" if method == "squash" else "false"),
                        "-F", "should_remove_source_branch=%s" % ("true" if delete_branch else "false"),
                        "-F", "merge_when_pipeline_succeeds=false") or {}
    if answer.get("state") != "merged":
        # Queued, or refused without an error: not merged, and said so.
        die("GitLab didn't merge it (%s)" % (answer.get("detailed_merge_status") or answer.get("state") or "no answer"), 77)
    print(json.dumps({"merged": number, "method": method, "deleted_branch": delete_branch}))


